      "solution": "import java.util.Scanner;\n\nclass Solution {\n    public static void main(String[] args) {\n        Scanner sc = new Scanner(System.in);\n        String s = sc.next();\n        System.out.println(new StringBuilder(s).reverse().toString().replaceFirst(\"^0+(?!$)\", \"\"));\n    }\n}",
      "statement": "Given an integer `n`, output its reverse.  \nIf the reversed number has leading zeros, remove them.\n\n### Examples:\n- Input: `123` → Output: `321`\n- Input: `100` → Output: `1`\n- Input: `-456` → Output: `-654`\n\n### Input\nA single integer `n`  \nConstraints: `-10^9 ≤ n ≤ 10^9`\n\n### Output\nThe reversed integer.",
